    "introduction": "St. James's Place provides wealth-management services through a network of financial advisers. Clients receive advice on areas such as investments, pensions and financial planning, with assets allocated to the group's range of investment solutions. Revenue is linked to advice and the ongoing administration and management of client money under its charging arrangements. Long-term adviser relationships are central to attracting and retaining customers. The business depends on client confidence, service quality and investment outcomes, while market movements affect the value of assets on which charges may be based. Regulation, the transparency of fees and the delivery of continuing advice are important operating considerations.",
